  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**\n   We address the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem by optimizing a step function on a grid to minimize the maximum overlap integral. Our method uses importance-aware binary optimization alongside continuous refinement. Unlike previous approaches focusing solely on continuous or binary forms, we combine structured initialization, local optimization, and adaptive restarts with periodic global exploration. The core innovation is prioritizing candidate evaluations based on potential improvement and automatically selecting resolution levels from initial solution snippets.\n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**\n   - **Representation**: h(x) is approximated by piecewise constant interpolation at n_points resolution, satisfying 0 \u2286 h \u2208 [0,1] and \u222b[0,2] h(x)dx = 1.\n   - **Objective**: Minimize C\u2085 = max\u2096 \u222b[h(x)(1-h(x+k))]dx\n   - **Implementation**: Evaluate via FFT-based correlation: compute_corr_scaled_fft(h) = max(|np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\"|) * (2/n_points)\n   - **Constraints**: Enforced using project_onto_box_sum(h, target_volume)\n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**\n   - **Phase 1: Initialization**\n     - Start with provided initial_h_values (n=512) and generate periodic-avoiding candidates:\n       - projects initial_h_values downsampled from Thue-Morse sequence\n       - generates random_binary_balanced patterns avoiding integer period structure\n     - Automatically checks any loaded initial_h_values from global scope and ensures feasibility via projection\n   \n   - **Phase 2: Core CMA-ES Optimization**\n     - Set generation_size=2, adaptive dimension reduction to max(n_points/64, 100)\n     - Warmstart with initial solution\n     - Implement population-based simplex restart (Nelder-Mead) every 300 function evaluations\n     - Fitness evaluation weights error and reconstruction feasibility proportionally\n   \n   - **Phase 3: Billion Variables Projection**\n     - Dynamically increases grid resolution to n_points\u00d78\n     - Coarse-to-fine multiscaling ensures feasibility at all levels\n     - Projection includes both box and integral constraints\n   \n   - **Phase 4: Adaptive Restart**\n     - Evaluate every 10 millionth candidate (or after 5 mins)\n     - Restart uses independent Gaussian initialization centered at global optimum\n     - Warm restart sets population to current_top_5 averaged across resolutions\n\n   - **Fallback Handling**\n     - Maintain rolling best solution from all resolutions\n     - If n_points > 5000, revert to feasible projection at budget end\n     - Compute C\u2085 via numpy.correlate for final validation\n\n4. **Search Choices and Useful Variations**\n   - **Resolution Management**: Automatically scans 3-5 standard resolutions (128, 256, 512, 1024)\n   - **Regressor Fields**: Uses temperature-scheduled random projection as exploration driver\n   - **Neighborhood Selection**: Adaptive dimension subsets via random projection for billion-variable problems\n   - **Restart Conditions**:\n     - Temporal: Every 30 mins if budget permits\n     - Performance: Only after achieving specified target reduction\n\n   - **Algorithm variants to consider**:\n     1. Dimension-Reflector mode (explores low-dimensional refinements)\n     2. Differential-reflection crossover (for population diversity)\n     3. Interval-Reflector projection (handles continuous solutions)\n\n5. **Numerical Robustness & Memory Use**\n   - **Feasibility**: project_onto_box_sum handles both box and box-constrained interpolation\n   - **Dimension Handling**: Ratio-aligned Stiefel projections maintain orthogonality in high-dimensional cases\n   - **Fallback Strategies**:\n     - NaN recovery via fallback candidate solutions\n     - Best solution preserves validity across resolution changes\n     - Memory checks trigger fallbacks at critical boundaries\n\n   - ** Statistical Regularization**:\n     - l\u2082-regularization for gradient descent restarts\n     - Additive noise to optimizers to escape local minima\n\n6. **Runtime Safeguards & Return Contract**\n   - **Time Tracking**: Strict budget enforcement with error recovery\n   - **Validation**: Verifies final candidate meets constraints via project_onto_box_sum\n   - **Output**:\n     - (h_final, computed_C\u2085_score, n_points_used)\n     - Final solution satisfies: min(h) > 0.9 or max(h) < 1.1 to ensure feasibility\n     - Computes all fitness metrics via provided correlation function\n     - Error tolerance: computes C\u2085 accounting for numerical roundoff\n\n   - **Implementation Safeguards**:\n     - Variable learning rates automatically compute via projected gradient descent\n     - Compute complexity bounds predictable via FFT scaling (n log n)\n     - Warm-only initialization for stability\n\n   - **Error Recovery**:\n     - Fallback materialized from current_top_5 if any\n     - If no top_5, returns line-aligned projection fallback\n     - Global backup candidate: mean-normalized exponential initializer",
